      "message": "kernel: make btck_LogEntry opaque\n\nAllows adding or changing fields without breaking the ABI, consistent\nwith other kernel objects. Strings are returned as btck_StringView.\n\nFields are now only converted when read, at the cost of a library call\nper field.\n\nThe logging callback may now call the btck_log_entry_get_* functions on\nits entry. They only read the entry, so they cannot deadlock.",
